  "userdoc": {
    "kind": "user",
    "methods": {},
    "notice": "One append-only version log per document (keyed by genesis), with an         agreement/offer layer over the SAME log — publishing and licensing are         one concern. Supersedes S2SPublicationModuleV2: the deal vocabulary         becomes agreement, reviewers are added, and read access moves behind         two explicit gates. Model:   - `makeOffer` is the single write authors use. It appends a version to the     log, then: whitelisted author (or safe) → the document becomes an     AGREEMENT immediately; anyone else → it becomes a pending OFFER. An author     can keep calling `makeOffer` to edit while it is still an offer (each call     appends a version) before the publication agrees.   - `admit` (onlySafe) promotes an offer to an agreement.   - Ending is asymmetric, and the two verbs are separate functions so a caller     cannot mean both:     - the author `retract`s. Terminal: `_ended` is set, the latest version is       tombstoned, the genesis is frozen and this publication can never strike       it again. Coming back means a new manuscript with a new genesis.     - the publication `reject`s. Not terminal: an agreement returns to the       pending offer set, an offer is declined, and the safe may accept again.     An ended genesis is frozen: `makeOffer` and `admit` revert. Its     versions stay on the ledger and remain readable through `getVersion`.   - `_append` does not gate the first version of a genesis. An untrusted     author can always leave a pending offer instead of reverting. After the     first version only the genesis author appends, so the publication cannot     write a version onto somebody else's genesis. Read gates (frozen signatures; sibling branches code against them):   - `canRead(genesis, reader)` — the safe, the genesis author and reviewers     all read a genesis once it is under an agreement or an offer; an unknown     genesis is never readable.   - `canReview(genesis, who)` — a reviewer, for an agreement or an offer. Three layers, deliberately separate:   - `canPublish(address)` is the whitelist predicate for \"may write into this     module at all\" — the safe, a whitelisted dev or a whitelisted author. It     is V2's body unchanged and nothing about agreements feeds it.   - `agreementsHeldBy` / `ownerHasAgreement(address)` answer a different,     per-author question: does this address currently hold any agreement with     this publication. It never grants publish rights.   - `canRead` / `canReview` are the per-genesis read gates: one manuscript,     one publication, one reader. Reviewers are an enumerable set capped at `MAX_REVIEWERS`, managed by the safe. A live proxy upgraded from V2 backfills `agreementsHeldBy` through `reinitializeV3`. Storage: `safe` is slot 101; 102–114 is V2's layout unchanged under the new agreement names (declaration order preserved); 115 `reviewers`, 116 `reviewerList`, 117 `agreementsHeldBy`, 118 `_ended`. Agreements and offers are enumerable sets of genesis pointing into the one log; `getAgreements`/`getOffers` read each entry's latest version via a cached pointer. Identity is bytes32 everywhere; the string→bytes32 conversion is owned by `shared` and used identically at write time and at the gate, so no on-chain cid map exists.",
    "version": 1
  }
